{
 "id": "cor-fd-l2-plancherel-middle-extension",
 "blueprint": {
  "is": "cor-fd-l2-plancherel-middle-extension",
  "from": null,
  "same_as": null
 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Plancherel for a middle extension: the transform shifts the weight of a pure lisse sheaf by exactly one",
 "statement": "Let $j:U_0\\hookrightarrow\\mathbf A^1_{k_0}$ be a dense open immersion\nwith finite complement, and let $\\mathcal M$ be a lisse Weil sheaf on\n$U_0$, punctually $\\iota$-pure\nof weight $w$. Suppose that the Fourier–Deligne transform of its\nmiddle extension has the\nmiddle-extension shape\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{FT}_\\psi\\bigl(j_*\\mathcal M[1]\\bigr)\\cong j'_*\\mathcal M'[1]\n$$\n\nwith $\\mathcal M'$ lisse on a dense open\n$U_0'\\hookrightarrow\\mathbf A^1_{k_0}$, punctually $\\iota$-pure of\nweight $v$. Then\n\n$$\nv=w+1 .\n$$\n\nThe middle-extension shape holds, with $\\mathcal M'$ irreducible,\nwhenever $\\mathcal M$ is irreducible and constituent-nonexceptional\n([prop-a1-fourier-middle-extension]). In that case the purity of\n$\\mathcal M'$ is automatic as well: if $\\mathcal M$ is nonzero,\nirreducible, constituent-nonexceptional and punctually $\\iota$-pure of\nweight $w$, then the sheaf $\\mathcal M'$ of\n[prop-a1-fourier-middle-extension] is punctually $\\iota$-pure of weight\nexactly $w+1$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-a1/sk-p-dl-a1-fourier-weight/cor-fd-l2-plancherel-middle-extension.md",
  "place": "node cor-fd-l2-plancherel-middle-extension, order 2779"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "prop-a1-fourier-middle-extension",
  "def-fd-transform",
  "def-weil-punctual-weights",
  "def-wf-l2-norm",
  "def-wf-middle-extension"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The trace function of [def-fd-trace-function] is unchanged in\nabsolute value by the shift $[1]$: the shift multiplies the\nalternating trace by $-1$, of $\\iota$-modulus one, so\n$\\|f_{j_*\\mathcal M[1]}\\|_m=\\|f_{j_*\\mathcal M}\\|_m$ and likewise\n$\\|f_{j'_*\\mathcal M'[1]}\\|_m=\\|f_{j'_*\\mathcal M'}\\|_m$ for every\n$m$. The Plancherel shift [lem-fd-l2-plancherel-shift], applied\nto the Weil complex $j_*\\mathcal M[1]$, therefore reads\n\n$$\n\\|j'_*\\mathcal M'\\|\n=\\bigl\\|\\operatorname{FT}_\\psi(j_*\\mathcal M[1])\\bigr\\|\n=\\|j_*\\mathcal M\\|+1 .\n$$",
   "uses": [
    "def-fd-trace-function",
    "lem-fd-l2-plancherel-shift"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "By the middle-extension comparison [lem-fd-l2-middle-extension],\n$\\|j_*\\mathcal M\\|=\\|\\mathcal M\\|=w$ and\n$\\|j'_*\\mathcal M'\\|=\\|\\mathcal M'\\|=v$, the second equality in each\ncase being the rigidity [lem-wf-l2-purity-rigidity] applied to the\npunctually pure lisse sheaf $\\mathcal M$ respectively $\\mathcal M'$.\nSubstituting, $v=w+1$.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-fd-l2-middle-extension",
    "lem-wf-l2-purity-rigidity"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "For the last assertion, [prop-a1-fourier-middle-extension] supplies the\nmiddle-extension shape with $\\mathcal M'$ lisse on the dense open\n$U'_0$, and [thm-fd-generic-fourier-sheaf-pure] shows that\n$\\mathcal M'$ is punctually $\\iota$-pure of some real weight $v$ on all\nof $U'_0$. All hypotheses of the first part are then met, so $v=w+1$.",
   "uses": [
    "prop-a1-fourier-middle-extension",
    "thm-fd-generic-fourier-sheaf-pure"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
